WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.380
Academia caught us

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.050
and forced us to participate 
in a survival duel.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.560
You are duelists of the modern era.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.840
Let your battle souls burn! Survive!

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.120
Devour the strong, and make 
them your flesh and blood!

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.760
Win and stand taller than anyone!

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.230
Glory on the Academia!

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.930
Glory on the Academia!

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.560
It's a special lesson, taught by 
cold-blooded Instructor Sanders,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.870
in which those who lose 
are turned into cards.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.200
Why?

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.780
Stay back! Get away!

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.200
Is this the end?

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:48.890
In that case...

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:52.040
That voice!

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:52.800
Tsukikage!

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:58.470
Friend or foe, all were turned 
into cards, one after the next.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.870
The Lancers...

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.920
And an eerie, beast-like being, 
concealing its face, challenged

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.510
Sawatari and me to a duel!

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.760
Who's there? Where are you?

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.180
Show yourself!

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.730
In a world split into four dimensions,

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:26.400
four boys exist, all with the same face.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.300
Their dragons call to each other,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.620
almost as if seeking one another.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:11.970
Battle Beast

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.960
He destroyed Academia's 
force in an instant.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.500
You must be kidding...

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.620
Where are you?

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.600
Come out, right now!

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.790
All destroyed?

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:39.030
Even my hand-picked elites 
could not surpass him?!

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.700
What's going on, here?

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.540
Who's "him"?

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.000
So there's another enemy, 
besides the Lancers?

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:49.240
C-Could it be... Battle Beast?

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:52.210
No way... That's just a silly rumor.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.940
A duel-starved animal that will 
fight anyone, ally or enemy,

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.970
and turn them into cards...

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.760
Then, it isn't just Tsukikage.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.920
The Academia students are also 
being turned into cards, one by one.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.950
Who is it?

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.690
The third party, aligned with neither 
us nor the Academia students?

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.020
I'm worried about Crow and Sawatari.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.370
We have to hurry and find them!

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:21.840
But in this dense jungle, 
we can't tell left from right.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:25.310
Okay.

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.030
Let's search the top of that pillar, then.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:36.880
Crow...

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.020
Find a way to get through this turn.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:42.740
And the... special, great, super, ultra...

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.900
abridged Shingo Sawatari will finish him off.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.110
Sorry, Sawatari.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.220
But you can't beat him.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:51.370
No...

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:53.840
I don't know if I can, either.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.070
But even if I can't...

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:57.980
Battle!

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.300
I attack Shingo Sawatari directly!

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.600
Huh? What?

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.690
Hey! Give me a break! 
What do you think you're doing?

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:17.160
I set one card and end my turn!

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.640
Damn you!

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.380
You'll pay for that!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.520
My turn!

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.550
Duel disk damaged.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.200
Forcible ejection of player from duel.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.350
What? My disk is broken?

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.360
Crow...

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.580
Was that deliberate?

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.800
Only one of us needs fight him.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.430
You get out of here.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.020
My turn!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:50.960
Now!

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.150
I activate my trap Blackwing — Last Will!

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:02.770
What happened?

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.530
C-Crow...

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.390
Did I do it?

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:30.770
No use, huh?

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.240
But I got you into the open.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.340
That's what our enemy looks like?

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:39.930
H-Hey...

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:41.400
Could it be him?

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.040
BB...

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.280
Wait, it really is?

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:50.480
A shame that my five elites 
could not surpass him,

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.350
but I'll have to the prioritize 
elimination of the Lancers.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.710
Watch carefully!

00:06:55.710 --> 00:07:00.230
That is the ultimate Battle Beast 
that I once personally trained...

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.700
Also known as BB!

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.970
Battle Beast?

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.300
"BB," he called him?

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.080
Crow!

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:09.270
Yuya?

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:20.450
Crow!

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.420
The rest is up to you, Yuya!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:25.890
Crow!

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.860
No!

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.530
Crow!

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:34.760
Frank.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:36.470
Amanda.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.160
Tanner.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.470
I'm sorry...

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.840
Crow!

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:56.590
How dare you do that to Crow?!

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.430
He did this to himself to save me...

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.380
Why do you always have to show off?!

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:18.080
Are you the one who beat Tsukikage?

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.280
And the Academia students, as well?

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.720
Answer me!

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.890
And if I did, what will you do?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.600
I'll make you pay!

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.860
I, the man Gongenzaka, feel the same way!

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.180
So do I, Shingo Sawatari!

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.200
It's totally broken, huh?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.400
Leave this to us!

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:44.570
We'll avenge Crow!

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:45.720
Duel!

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:50.810
I summon Gladiator Beast 
Laquari from my hand!

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:00.230
I assume you have all heard the rumors.

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:02.830
BB is a defective product who so loved battle,

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:05.370
he would turn both ally and enemy into cards.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:08.560
Therefore, I kept him in 
prolonged confinement...

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.680
And during that time, I raised all of you

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.030
to become the true ultimate duelists.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:17.050
But now, you've seen the results!

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:20.240
My five chosen elites were 
effortlessly defeated.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:22.350
You will all be next!

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:25.810
If you wish to not be turned 
into cards, like those five,

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:28.450
burn his duel into your eyes!

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:29.750
Yes, sir!

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:33.830
I set three cards and end my turn.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.290
My turn!

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:40.570
I set the Pendulum Scale with

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:45.860
Scale 6 Performapal Shieldrummer and 
Scale 8 Performapal Odd-Eyes Unicorn!

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:59.540
Now I can summon Level 7 
monsters simultaneously!

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.510
Swing, my soul's pendulum.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.480
Draw a shining arc in the sky!

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:07.100
Pendulum Summon!

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:08.300
Appear!

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:13.150
The heroic one with beautiful, 
different-colored eyes,

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.670
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.660
Pendulum Summon...

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.190
Let's go.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:24.400
I attack Laquari with Odd-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon!

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.370
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:30.840
Continuous Trap Gladiator 
Beast's Medallion!

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:35.370
Gladiator Beasts on my field 
can't be destroyed by battle.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.520
But battle damage is doubled.

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:45.020
After they do battle, I can swap a Gladiator 
Beast with another in my deck!

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:50.660
I Special Summon Gladiator 
Beast Secutor from my deck!

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.810
Monsters he can swap out 
after they do battle...

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:04.240
Is that why he chose to 
take that big damage?

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:08.510
But I can't imagine what effect it 
might have, to be worth the risk.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:11.130
Just what is he trying to do?

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:12.870
I end my turn.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:17.960
My turn.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.900
Draw!

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:23.900
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 1

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:28.460
Superheavy Samurai General Jade and 
Scale 8 Superheavy Samurai General Coral!

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:35.690
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:38.480
Pendulum Summon!

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:39.910
Appear!

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:47.320
Tuner Monster Superheavy 
Samurai Battleball.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.790
Superheavy Samurai Soulfire Suit!

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:54.250
Superheavy Samurai Prepped Defense!

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.700
Three at once?

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:07.000
Level 2 Battleball tunes Level 2 
Superheavy Samurai Soulfire Suit

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:09.970
and Level 3 Prepped Defense!

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:14.320
Swift as the wind. Silent as the forest.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.980
Ninja, soundlessly strike the final blow.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:19.120
Synchro Summon!

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:24.220
Appear, Level 7 Superheavy 
Samurai Stealth Ninja!

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.670
Be careful, Gongenzaka.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:34.200
His monsters appear to have effects 
that activate when they do battle.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.470
Yeah...

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:38.400
And with my immovable duel, 
I'll send them flying.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.490
Superheavy Samurai Stealth Ninja

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:43.370
can attack from defense position, 
using its defense points!

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:45.090
Have you forgotten that

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:48.990
Continuous Trap Gladiator Beast's 
Medallion's effect means

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:52.350
that my Gladiator Beasts can't 
be destroyed by battle?

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:54.840
Superheavy Samurai Stealth Ninja

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:58.750
can halve its defense points 
to attack you directly

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:01.290
during the Battle Phase!

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:03.710
Great one!

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:06.460
Now, its monster's effect won't activate!

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:11.670
I activate my Continuous Trap 
Gladiator Beast's Valor.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.480
When I have a Gladiator Beast on the field,

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:17.960
your monsters can attack only Gladiator Beasts.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:18.880
What?

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:22.990
And my Continuous Trap Gladiator 
Beast's Medallion prevents

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:24.850
Secutor's destruction by battle.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:31.320
I attacked him directly, but he turned 
it into attack against his monster.

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.190
The real surprise is yet to come.

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:38.660
You've awakened a battle-starved monster.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:40.970
My Gladiator Beast's effect.

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:45.140
After a Battle Phase in which a Secutor 
I Special Summoned fought,

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:50.110
I can Special Summon two Gladiator 
Beasts, other than Secutor!

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:54.080
I Special Summon an attack-position 
Gladiator Beast Augustus

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.810
and a defense-position Murmillo!

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:02.250
Now, he has two more Gladiator Beasts?

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:07.100
When Augustus is Special Summoned 
through a Gladiator Beast's effect,

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:12.500
I can Special Summon one Gladiator Beast 
from my hand, in defense position.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:14.040
What?

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.730
Another Special Summon?

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:18.470
I summon another Murmillo.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:26.640
When Murmillo is Special Summoned 
through a Gladiator Beast's effect,

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:29.680
I can destroy one monster on the field.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.820
With the first Murmillo's effect,

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:35.830
I destroy Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:40.830
In that instant, I activate Continuous 
Trap Thumbs Down.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:45.760
For every card destroyed, 
I deal 500 damage to you.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:54.870
And the second Murmillo's effect 
destroys Stealth Ninja!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:15:00.870
In that instant, Continuous Trap 
Thumbs Down's effect activates!

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.220
He's in total control...

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:10.690
And all of that was on Gongenzaka's turn.

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:14.570
Using my attack as the trigger

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:17.880
to activate his monster's effects to that degree...

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:19.130
I end my turn!

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:20.880
During my End Phase,

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:24.280
since Stealth Ninja was destroyed by an effect,

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:26.910
it can be Special Summoned 
from my graveyard!

00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:30.970
Augustus's effect ceases 
during my End Phase,

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:33.640
and the second Murmillo returns to my deck.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:37.980
I'm sorry, Yuya. Your Odd-Eyes...

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:40.450
Hey, we aren't finished yet.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.890
My turn!

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:47.720
By sending the necessary cards to my deck,

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:50.560
I can Fusion Summon a Gladiator Beast 
without a Polymerization card.

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:51.760
What?

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:57.470
I fuse Gladiator Beasts Augustus, 
Murmillo, and Secutor.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:01.130
Spirits of ancient, fallen warriors,

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:05.420
assemble in the name of your emperor, 
and show your power!

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:06.680
Fusion Summon.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:13.610
Come on, Gladiator Beast Andabata!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.710
I activate Andabata's effect.

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:23.320
When I successfully Fusion Summon it, 
I can Special Summon

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:27.700
a Gladiator Beast Fusion Monster from 
my Extra Deck, other than Andabata.

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:31.770
Come out, Gladiator Beast Gyzarus!

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:36.990
Next, I can activate Gyzarus's effect...

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:39.880
When I successfully Special Summon Gyzarus,

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:43.400
I can destroy up to two cards on the field!

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:49.390
I choose Superheavy Samurai 
Stealth Ninja and Shieldrummer.

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:53.660
In that instant, the effect of Thumbs Down

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:56.760
deals 500 points of damage to both of you.

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:04.920
A thorough combo duel, with monster 
and trap effects working in tandem...

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.800
Was this his goal?

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:08.840
This is bad...

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:12.010
Neither Yuya nor Gongenzaka 
has a monster on the field!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:15.980
Now, which of you will be food for Gyzarus?

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.490
Will it be me or Gongenzaka?

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:21.950
Whichever, we have no choice but to 
break through with Action Cards.

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:24.970
But Gongenzaka...

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:29.830
Hey, decide already! Stop stalling!

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:31.060
Yuya...

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:33.300
Why is he in such a hurry?

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:34.870
I've decided...

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:37.940
First, I'll attack you directly!

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:41.060
Go, Gyzarus!

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:56.620
I see...

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:00.700
Gongenzaka fights an immovable duel. 
He can't use Action Cards.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:04.030
That's why Yuya intentionally 
made himself the target.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.770
Yuya, you...

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:13.340
Andabata's effect returns Gyzarus to 
my Extra Deck, once it does battle,

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:17.710
and adds that Gyzarus's attack 
points to its own.

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:20.190
3400 attack points?

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:24.620
At that rate, he could take Yuya or 
Gongenzaka out with one hit.

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:26.520
Are you ready?

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:28.990
Yuya!

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:33.160
Go ahead and try to get an Action Card.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:36.830
Andabata attacks you directly!

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:53.050
Action Spell Benkei Guard!

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:56.610
I Special Summon one Benkei 
Token in attack position!

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:00.350
You cannot attack anything 
but this Benkei Token,

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:02.820
and this token cannot be destroyed by battle!

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.190
Gongenzaka!

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:10.740
Gongenzaka...

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.160
He picked up an Action Card?

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:14.650
Gongenzaka...

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:18.400
By doing that, you can't use your deck!

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:21.920
You saved me first.

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:24.230
I'm simply returning the favor.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:27.380
That is the way of the Gongenzaka Dojo.

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:29.950
I activate Andabata's effect.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:31.580
When the Battle Phase ends,

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.200
I can return this card to my Extra Deck,

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:38.320
to Special Summon two Gladiator 
Beasts from my deck!

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:43.030
Come out, Gladiator Beasts 
Murmillo and Bestiari.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:46.080
A token that can't be destroyed by battle, eh?

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:49.000
Then, I activate Murmillo's effect!

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:54.870
The Benkei Token can't be destroyed 
by monster effects, either!

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:57.140
From now on,

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:59.890
I, the man Gongenzaka, shall face you.

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:02.080
You will not lay one hand on Yuya!

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:03.700
Gongenzaka...

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:07.400
We'll see about that.

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:09.520
I activate Bestiari's effect.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:13.690
I destroy Odd-Eyes Unicorn 
in the Pendulum Zone!

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:18.320
And Continuous Trap Thumbs Down's effect.

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:22.400
I deal 500 damage to the player 
of the destroyed card!

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:30.270
Damn you, attacking Yuya, 
who's defenseless...

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:34.980
You're an eyesore, so disappear.

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:39.680
I send Bestiari and Murmillo 
to my deck and fuse them!

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:42.520
Bird of prey warrior from ancient times,

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:46.660
merge your soul with the swordsman, 
and become the storied hero!

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:48.390
Fusion Summon!

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:52.600
Come, Gladiator Beast Gyzarus!

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:54.800
I activate Gyzarus's effect!

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:57.770
I destroy two cards on the field.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.600
Two? But the only ones left are...

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:09.080
And for each card destroyed 
with Thumbs Down's effect,

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:13.720
I deal 500 points of damage to you!

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.890
Gongenzaka!

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.360
Gongenzaka!

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:39.830
Go, Yuya.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:42.780
Even alone, you... You should...

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:49.070
Hold on.

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:50.950
I'll turn you into a card now.

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:53.920
Gongenzaka!

00:23:49.520 --> 00:23:51.630
Are you the one who defeated Crow?

00:23:51.630 --> 00:23:53.070
And if I am?

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:54.080
I'll make you pay.

00:23:54.080 --> 00:23:57.780
For the sake of the children who 
saw me off, I will crush you!

00:23:58.090 --> 00:23:59.280
Interesting.

00:23:59.280 --> 00:24:03.740
To talk that big, he must be quite confident.

00:24:03.740 --> 00:24:05.880
Show me, then...

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:08.930
Show me how you stand against 
the strongest Battle Beast

00:24:08.930 --> 00:24:11.400
that I raised at Academia!

00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:15.420
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Stigma of Misfortune.

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:17.660
The fun is only getting started!
